  "compatibility": {
    "maximum_selection": "New opcode tag 16 uses binary container version 4. Historical v2/v3 bytes unchanged; old versions reject the new tag. Existing symbolic numeric profiles keep their earlier basis policy.",
    "finite_checked_execution": "General operation entrypoint explicitly permits checked finite native address arithmetic, maximum and exact buffer loads. It does not infer that arbitrary native arithmetic represents addresses; compiler taint/oracle tests verify generated attention/MLP.",
    "legacy_attention": "One query head and one KV token, with complete dot/scale/softmax/weighted arithmetic. Configurable scratch adds multi-token attention.",
    "legacy_mlp": "Square FFN and recomputation O(embedding^2*FFN); three loop levels require HotLoop/Runtime. Scratch plan uses four complete blocks, O(embedding*FFN), and at most two levels.",
    "legacy_layer": "One head, position zero, square FFN, epsilon=1e-5, RoPE base=10000, stride=embedding; input is a slot and learned tensor bases are absolute. Reserve scratch/KV at input_slot+1..+17, output at input_slot+18. Legacy column-constant argument is retained but owned configuration supplies the stride.",
    "numerical_domains": "Bounded profiles remain partial; checked construction does not inspect runtime data. Callers must satisfy declarations and use matching allocated layouts. Layer KV is f64, not the independent model runtime F32 cache.",
    "configuration_folding": "Only closed MLP configuration sub-DAGs are evaluated at compilation with Basis::Bml.apply_real. Tests preserve original DAG bits for default/custom configurations; no activations or learned weights are folded."
